    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Rouran ruled the Mongolian steppe from 402 to 552 as a confederation led by the Yujiulü clan.</li><li>Their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yujiulu-shelun">Shelun</a> is the first ruler recorded as using khagan as the title of a supreme steppe sovereign.</li><li>Their Turkic ironworkers under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bumin-qaghan">Bumin</a> revolted in 552, destroying the khaganate and founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-turkic-khaganate">Turkic Khaganate</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Northern Wei emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taiwu-of-northern-wei">Taiwu</a> ordered that the Rouran be called 'Ruanruan', meaning 'wriggling insects', as a deliberate insult.</p></aside>
    </section>

